+# Aegis LLM Support — vLLM/Triton + gateway streaming + RAG + red-team
+
+This directory contains:
+- Helm skeleton for deploying vLLM (ops/llm_support/helm/vllm)
+- Streaming gateway proxy with incremental safety checks and DP token accounting (ops/llm_support/gateway)
+- Lightweight safety-on-stream helper (safety_stream_checker.py)
+- Red-team LLM tests (ops/llm_support/redteam) and a GH Action workflow (llm_redteam.yml)
+- RAG integration: Milvus deployment manifest and a simple embedding service (ops/llm_support/rag)
+
+How to use (quick):
+1. Edit Helm values (registry, nodeSelector, storage class) and deploy vLLM:
+   helm install aegis-vllm ops/llm_support/helm/vllm -n model-serving
+2. Deploy the streaming gateway (build and push image then apply a k8s Deployment pointing at streaming_proxy.py)
+3. Deploy Milvus and embedding service if you need RAG.
+4. Run red-team GH Action or run tests locally by setting MODEL_ENDPOINT env.
+
+Notes:
+- Replace placeholders (YOUR_REGISTRY, model paths, storage classes) before production.
+- The streaming proxy implements a conservative incremental safety check; full analysis is performed by the orchestrator/Argo evidence workflows.
+- For production LLMs, tune batching, GPU types, and add autoscaling.
+
